if we have collisions, and we want to store items directly on our arrays
(don't use chaining, in other words don't use nested linked-list)
we should use open-addressing
(open a new address on current array)

we have some different ways to do this
1.linear probing
2.quadratic probing
3.double hashing

Note: we use same algorithm, when we want to find the value
      it means we start from base index, and move to next one (based on the function we used for probing)
      and check if he is the key or not?
      like chaining, we should traverse the linked-list,
      we should chek all index we passed by open addressing.
      (check by key)

Note: deleting on open addressing should be done carefully,
      if we just delete some index, and make it null
      it could be generate some problems.
      because when we are searching for a key, when we see a null index, our search will terminate
      (because if we see free index, it means we have not any new key that open addressing
       need to fill it)
      so to prevent this problem, when we delete something we fill it by something like "deleted"
      so on searching, he see this index as not null index and keep searching,
      but it is free for new insert!


Note: if we have a hash function that have not any collision (it is not possible)
      we can just store values without keys!
      but in real world due to collisions, we store (k,v) on
      indexes and linked-list to check the key!
      in chaining we need key
      in open addressing we need key


summary:
        linear      : nextIndex = (h(k) + i) % table_size)          i
        quadratic   : nextIndex = (h(k) + i^2) % table_size         i^2
        double hash : nextIndex = (h(k) + i * h2(k)) % table_size   i*h2(k)
